        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-6 md:p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            MuscleTech protein powder is a solid mid-priced whey, and Nitro-Tech is its best tub: 30 g of protein and 3 g of creatine per scoop for about $1.57 per 25 g at the Amazon price we saw. Whey Gold is the plain-whey alternative at about $1.49, Grass-Fed is the pick without artificial sweeteners, and 100% Mass Gainer is the gainer with a clean lead result, per MuscleTech.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            The weak spot is certification. MuscleTech relies on cGMP manufacturing and HPLC-tested creatine rather than an NSF or Informed badge, so tested athletes should look elsewhere. Everyone else can buy the largest tub they will finish, wait for a sale, and check the label on the tub they receive, since MuscleTech revises its formulas often.
